{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/477696-your-least-liked-compacts-conspiracies-and-why","id":477696,"title":"Your least liked Compacts/Conspiracies, and why?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-12T02:36:15-07:00","id":477696,"title":"Your least liked Compacts/Conspiracies, and why?","content":"The Vigil contains a wide variety of Compacts and Conspiracies. Whilst this allows for a truly remarkable array of ideas to be covered, let's face it: they can't all be gems. So, I was morbidly curious: what are the Compacts and/or Conspiracies that, for you personally, rang as &quot;duds&quot;, and why?<br /> <br /> For myself...<br /> <br /> The Keepers of the Source immediately springs to mind. They are just too unbelievable, in my mind. Homicidal hippies? Motivated by the fact that they're united by a particularly sucky variant of Unseen Senses that manifests as &quot;feels pain when near loci and Essence holders&quot;? A Cell with that sort of background, but it just strains my sense of disbelief that they A: have had the numbers of implied sensitives amongst their membership to develop as a faction, and B: not wound up dead as a result of picking fights with werewolves and mages.<br /> <br /> Ashwood Abbey is another obvious one. I get the whole black and gray morality thing, but from the start, these guys were just handled too poorly. They're the obvious bad guys - like saying Belial's Brood is one of the core player factions in Requiem. They had some interesting ideas, but they were just too hamfistedly the &quot;token evil teammate&quot; of the original C&amp;Cs. And considering this same set includes the Malleus Maleficarium, whom I have personal reasons for *hating*, that the Abbey sticks out as my &quot;#1 least liked corebook faction&quot; is saying something.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, although I have very personal reasons for detesting the Malleus Maleficarium, the Long Night and Les Mysteres, I don't think I would include them here. This is because I do not think they are *bad* factions - in fact, I recognize all too well that they are natural, obvious factions to include in a game like Hunter. I just personally find them highly unappealing.<br /> <br /> ...Those are the only two factions that immediately come to mind when I think about &quot;what Hunter factions do I not like&quot;. So, what factions do other people find unappealing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T10:00:47-07:00","id":478052,"title":"","content":"amm.. the Hunt Club kinda jump to my mind, but I always thought about them as more of an NPC material...<br /> <br /> Other then that, I like most of the organizations. The Night Watch and the Les Voyageurs are the two groups I find the most unappealing, and even there I can think about some cool things I could do with them. The Ashwood Abbey and the Keepers are actually among my favorite groups in hunter, with only the Lucifuge and the Knights of Saint George topping them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T10:39:21-07:00","id":478104,"title":"","content":"The Cainite Heresy. I'm a big fan of Ashwood Abbey.<br /> <br /> It seems like with the Cainite Heresy they went to great lengths to mesh it into the history of the setting in a way few other conspiracies were, having ties to the Aves of Minerva as well as the Requiem for Rome books. Their write-up has theories for how other conspiracies can find out about them because they've had contact throughout the years. They even played a part in one of the stories in the Strix fiction anthology. It may even be a shout out to Vampire the Masquerade. They have a wide variety of powers that are incredibly useful against their opponents, a mystery behind them to investigate. They even have good reasons for being so focused. While I love the Knights of St George, they're depicted as incredibly misguided and some people think they're even corrupted by evil aliens because if you just look at a Mage book, you can see they're wrong. And Les Mysteres are a bunch of do-gooders trying to kill the Forsaken, many of whom are trying to protect the world in turn. Vampires are easy to justify hunting, though. For every 'good one,' there's at least one sire who killed them in the first place and likely another two who would drain someone dry without a second thought if they thought it would give them an edge.<br /> <br /> But in addition to not playing well with others, they're, 'a crazy suicide-cult' of extremists who offer no compromise. It's just limiting from an options standpoint. There's things you can do with them, but they're unappealing to potential players due to the fanaticism.<br /> <br /> And also while I like the Promethean Brotherhood and the Faithful of Shulpae, and I'm not a 'balance guy,' I find it annoying that they have such a similar power while one is demonstrably better. This is fixed with a house rule, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-12-2015, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T14:37:54-07:00","id":478311,"title":"","content":"The Abby, for sick good times seems like weak justification to put your life in danger hunting monsters.<br /> my head cannon warps the Abby into a monster summoning sex cult, working for a Nyarlathotep like entity . makes more sense plays on their themes which are already super antagonistic, but ultimately their not really hunters.<br /> <br /> I'm having trouble thinking of any other Compact or Conspiracy I don't like or would change whole cloth; although I would/do build on all of them. things like making the Promethean Brotherhood a full blown Conspiracy and allowing them to take magic from other supernaturals. or making the Cainites less suicidal but with still a very terrorist-like vibe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T15:13:33-07:00","id":478344,"title":"","content":"None of my orgs so far, that's good <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> anyway I've got quite a few opinions (where else does the fanwork come from).<br /> <br /> <br /> Firstly I really dislike the idea of Hunters orgs that are pawns of the supernatural. Does it happen, sure, all the time. But it's antagonist material and it really bugs me to see it in the protagonist section. So we have:<br /> <br /> <b>Les Mysteries - </b>Aside from being manipulated by spirits into fighting werewolves they're not really that bad. I'm not too fond of the genericness they have though, voodoo hunters, native American shaman hunters, Christian ecstatic hunters, alien abductees: All great ideas, but wrapping them into one Conspiracy robs them of their chance to shine individually. Most of all though, I feel there was a missed opportunity. Their Endowment is about a harmonious union of flesh and spirit, that's the exact opposite of the Werewolves enforcement of the gauntlet. It makes a far more interesting conflict than Spirits tricking them into fighting.<br /> <br /> <b>Division Six</b> <b>-</b> I honestly feel that this is just a poor taste insult at technocracy fans. The picture of the sample hunter is what really gives me this impression (fun fact, I wrote the reality hackers specifically so I could portray someone who looks like that sample hunter as totally awesome). Fundamentally the Technocracy doesn't work as a Compact. Their whole shtick is that they're a world controlling Conspiracy and their concepts of &quot;reality deviant&quot; and similar need an Endowment, at the minimum, to let players say them with conviction.<br /> <br /> <b>The Knights of St George - </b>It's been a while since I read them, but I have a distinct impression that they're actually under the control of the Faceless Angels, or the control of something. More than that, I just don't feel engaged by them. They fight witches, they have an Endowment, they're secretive, they're a cult. And? They don't really engage with any larger themes, certainly not Witch Finder's stated themes of moral ambiguity.<br /> <br /> I'm not putting VALKYRIE here because it's easy to cut out the vampire nonsense (I prefer to say that vampires are metaphorical Afghanistan warlords to TF:V's USA) or the Malleus because I consider Ghouls and anything with an unmodified Morality/Integrity trait to be human. (If you're curious about how I justify the Athenic Church - simple. They're for Hunter: Cults, the usual rules don't apply).<br /> <br /> <br /> Organisations who're founded on an inaccuracy, for lack of a better word. A group like the Promethian Brotherhood are evil, but their founding purpose is to steal magic and they're competent at stealing magic. In contrast <b>The Keepers of the Source </b>Are founded to protect Mother Earth from witches draining source. However draining source does not harm Earth. Nothing in the Mage or the Hunter rules says it does. I don't mind the homicidal hippies angle, it's twisted in a great way, but they need a better reason to be homicidal. I make them competent at manipulating lay lines to promote peace and love, and willing to kill any Witch who tries to steal their lay lines or nexuses.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not a fan of <b>Heritage House</b> simply because I believe uniting all hunters misses the point. And worse, it's boring, the differences between goals and motivations is what makes the setting easier. The Scarlet Watch is a much better take on the idea of Vigil as a family business.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Doubting Souls: It feels like Les Voyagers started with the idea of a Mountain Main / Fur Trapper as a Hunter (a good idea). But since there wasn't any room in the book for an individual Tier One hunter/Cell, they turned it into a Compact without doing anything to actually turn him into Tier 2. No origin, organisation, or reason for actually being a Compact. The economics of Les Voyagers don't make much sense either. They're in it to sell monster parts, but they're basically broke. If monsters aren't worth top dollar, why do they risk their lives instead of safer prey?<br /> <hr /><br /> BTW. I actually like the Canites because they're great Vampire foils. They're the abused to vampire's abusers. They're (often nomadic) outsiders while Vampire often are The Man in the penthouse. Vampires are treated as pawns by their superiors, the Canites are given help by their &quot;superiors&quot; no strings attached (well maybe, who knows). Vampires power their magic by stealing blood, Cainites power their magic by donating blood. Vampire culture is dysfuctional and violent against fellow vampires, Canite culture is... dysfunctional but Canites genuinely have each others back.<br /> <br /> This kind of relaitionship with the hunter and prey being different takes on the same core idea: abuse -&gt; abuser / abused. It's something I really like and tried to capture a lot of when I did a Hunter splatbook. Look at the Lord Stewards compared to the Lost: The Lost are seeking a home - a community, the Lord Stewards maintain community and heritage on a national scale. Changeling powers come from contracts, which they twist and look for loopholes. Steward powers come from contracts, which they honour in spirit as well as word (same parallel with Pledges). Changelings were victimised by a god-powered and fundamentally alien being. The Lord Stewards have a working and mutually friendly business relationship with an aspect of the Wyrd, so a god-powered and fundamentally alien being. The Lost are very good at hiding, the Stewards are semi-public.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T15:29:14-07:00","id":478365,"title":"","content":"AKD and TFV. I hate acronyms. Actually my issue with them is that I like to have a good idea of the logisitics of conspiracies, and neither really does that; both treat it as more a black box for players to recieve stuff from. I get the game reasons for that, but it niggles at me. TFV wasn't helped by my reading Delta Green at about the same time because that really put a massive amount of space (which Hunter simply doesn't have) into explaining how the various conspiracies work, to the point that it kinda ruined my ability to suspend disbelief with TFV where a lot is handwaved in order to make the game work.<br /> <br /> Also, both have really long histories without any real attempt to justify it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T19:03:53-07:00","id":478596,"title":"","content":"If I had to hate on any compact or conspiracy, I'd probably pick the Malleus Maleficarum, which is funny, because I kind of like them the most too.<br /> <br /> I've ranted about it before, but the Malleus's focus is on vampires. A holy order whose sacred text says &quot;Thou shalt not suffer a witch to live&quot; and whose name is quite literally &quot;the Hammer of Witches&quot;... Focuses on vampires. An order founded in a religious tradition that still practices exorcism and says that witchcraft can unleash demons upon people focuses on vampires. An order whose religious heads have set forth decrees stating that signs of demonic possession include supernatural knowledge and abilities hunts vampires. Okay, maybe that last one a bit.<br /> <br /> I could go on. The Malleus's focus feels off. They should be omnivores of the supernatural, sure, but their primary focus should be witches. A part of this is practical - if you believe that witches are the primary mechanism by which evil enters the world, killing a vampire is just putting a compress on a bleeding wound - but a part of it is theological too: Vampires, werewolves, and the like are victims of demonic possession and, therefore, either deserve destruction or exorcism; their choices are not their own. Witches, however, have free will. The receiving of the Great Commission, the duty of all Christians to go out and witness to the world, requires the Malleus to simultaneously try and save the souls of those who can be redeemed from witchcraft and to destroy those who are truly devil-bought.<br /> <br /> Another good reason this should be the focus is the obvious fact that it allows for really clear schisms within the Malleus. I do want to say that I love vampires as threats for religious Hunters because the siren's call of the pleasures of the flesh is an awesome counterpoint to unworldly characters, but, at an organizational level, there's not going to be any interesting internal conflicts around this. They might argue whether vampires need to be destroyed, exorcised, or can somehow be redeemed/controlled - sort of a theological equivalent to Fuck/Marry/Kill (egads, why is that even a thing?) - but that's a schism every Hunter faces; not really a unique one to the Malleus.<br /> <br /> No, if the Malleus's chief opponent is witches, it raises foundational questions about the Malleus itself. How would you tell the difference between a sorcerer and a true miracle worker sent by God? Plenty of the Obrimos Path amongst the Awakened certainly feel like they saw God (or something like it). How can you tell the difference? Is there such a thing as &quot;holy&quot; magic? What difference is there between the workings of a sorcerer and the Malleus's benedictions?<br /> <br /> Phew. Think that's all of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T21:50:29-07:00","id":478799,"title":"","content":"Every time Task Force: VALKYRIE comes up I ask myself if I could be better served by just snatching up their Advanced Armory options and importing Delta Green into the World of Darkness instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T06:58:59-07:00","id":479023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/477696-your-least-liked-compacts-conspiracies-and-why#post477696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ashwood Abbey is another obvious one. I get the whole black and gray morality thing, but from the start, these guys were just handled too poorly. They're the obvious bad guys - like saying Belial's Brood is one of the core player factions in Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer the Bear Lodge from Spirit Slayers - they're hunters (in the Vigil sense) to prove they're great hunters (in the general sense) - that could have satisfied the thrill-seeking side of Ashwood Abbey, as well as fitting their demographic origin, without the over the top side. Enough hunters - even destroy all monsters types - would find &quot;proving I'm a badass hunter&quot; a contemptible motive that such an Abbey would still fit the disliked-group niche (ironically, many werewolves, in whom the Bear Lodge specialises, would find it a perfectly reasonable motive).<br /> <br /> I agree with KingsRaven about Les Mysteres, but for not for all the same reasons. For me it's just the generic part. Groups who see their spirits as loa, angels, or aliens, wouldn't see themselves as the same group just because their Endowment is the same. Being manipulated by the spirits rather than in harmony with them doesn't bother me though - there's no other version of the Hisil where relationships like that are harmonious, and having one here would feel odd.<br /> (More generally, I don't require every hunter group to be stalwart, informed, and free of supernatural influence).<br /> <br /> There aren't any others I dislike. The Faithful of Shulpae maybe, but that's mostly because there are other types of group I'd rather have seen than any animus against them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T08:03:22-07:00","id":479045,"title":"","content":"I actually like all of the conspiracies. I dont really think any of them are handeled poorly. They are all their own flavor of spice, you can sprinkle on the meal that is your game. If you use them all, your meal will seem too spiced, and it'll clash horribly. Some spices compliment each other and some spices dont go well together, but no one spice is entirely horrid.<br /> <br /> That said, I feel like the one thats alittle off in my books, are The Ascending Ones. Their origin are in badass egyptian supernatural task force, kinda like the middle eastern Task Force Valkyrie or Malleus Malefictum of their day. But all that awesome badassery kinda gets jettisoned in favor of supernatural drug addicts/drug cartel. Thats an interesting concept, but I find it alittle too silly to deploy with any reasonable degree of success. Kinda like the Keepers of the Source that OP mentioned. A cool enough concept, but alittle too silly to be deployable very often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T10:05:31-07:00","id":479213,"title":"","content":"I've always wondered what would happen to a Keeper of the Source if they somehow ended up in the Shadow. Essence pools as far as the eye can see, and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T11:24:55-07:00","id":479303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/477696-your-least-liked-compacts-conspiracies-and-why?p=479213#post479213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always wondered what would happen to a Keeper of the Source if they somehow ended up in the Shadow. Essence pools as far as the eye can see, and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div> Or what happens if they Awaken. Do they continue to live a life of suffering, or does it &quot;iron the kinks out&quot;, per say?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T11:27:45-07:00","id":479304,"title":"","content":"They might turn into Banishers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T02:12:52-07:00","id":480021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/477696-your-least-liked-compacts-conspiracies-and-why?p=479213#post479213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always wondered what would happen to a Keeper of the Source if they somehow ended up in the Shadow. Essence pools as far as the eye can see, and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div> Nothing, considering they have unseen sense- source, and witches are the only creatures that use source. <br /> <br /> Even if, in a crossover campaign, you made witches and mages the same thing, that would still make source equal to mana, which as far as I know is no more plentiful in the shadow than the material world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T02:35:55-07:00","id":480028,"title":"","content":"I's pretty clear that &quot;source pools&quot; include both hallows and loci. They're mentioned getting ripped apart by werewolves on several occasions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T21:41:07-07:00","id":481920,"title":"","content":"The one conspiracy I've just never been able to do anything with, to the point that I frequently forget they exist, is the Ascending Ones. Their aesthetic isn't particularly compelling or memorable, and their hodge-podge of influences kind of dilutes whatever theme it was they were looking for. <br /> <br /> Aegis Kai Doru has also never really floated my boat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T01:01:27-07:00","id":482116,"title":"","content":"<b>Ashwood Abbey</b>: There like the Hunter ver. of &quot;Jackass&quot; but with more money and amoral depravity if not stupidity. As cool as that may sound. Risking , life, limb, sanity and even your very soul for kicks and lols. Just sounds idiotic. Kind of a slap to the face of most hunters that are risking their lives for their families, friends, and humanity. Yeah their not my cup of tea. But i do believe there good to show, how bad and shallow hunters can be. If not utterly crazy. <br /> <br /> <b>Null Mysteriis</b>: When your in a world full of Vampires, Werewolves, Ghosts and Fairy folk. Disbelief just seem silly. Granted there whole stick is about Scientific methods proving everything they believe is right and disregarding everything else. Feels too condescending to me. They maybe good for a more practical hunter outlook ,but they seem dry and uninteresting . Though them meeting a Threnodist mage would make their heads explode. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Team Force Valkyrie</b> : The G. I. Joe's of WOD. Pretty kickass in there own right. But for me they seem like the guys that just cover up everything, &quot;neutralize&quot; the situation, and possibly kidnap and or erase certain people if given the orders to. A shocktroop that takes care of supernatural problems or possible problems. I treat them more like a neutral group of hunters/cleaners. They don't need a code of morality or sense of justice. They don't need to answer to any other group really. &quot;Just following orders&quot; could be enough reason for them to do all kinds of horrible or unethical things. I look at them as a really grey hunting group that you would rather stay out of their way than to ever involve yourself with. In that sense. This is why i much prefer the Vanguard over them.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T03:19:23-07:00","id":482183,"title":"","content":"Nth'ing <b>Ashwood Abbey</b>. I get what they're going for, I just don't feel like its interesting enough to devote an entire Compact to. Honestly, when 2E rolls around I'd like to see their wordcount given to one of the more interesting groups from the supplements (VASCU, Bear Lodge, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T04:34:18-07:00","id":482210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\